## 1. Project Overview

The **Resume Screening & Recruitment Analytics** project explores candidate characteristics and recorded hiring outcomes using data analytics and business intelligence tools.

The project uses a dataset containing approximately 200,000 candidate records. Python and Pandas are used for data preparation and exploratory data analysis, PostgreSQL and SQL are used to investigate candidate groups, and Microsoft Power BI is used to develop interactive dashboards.

The purpose is to transform raw candidate data into understandable metrics, visualizations, and evidence-based business insights.

The project demonstrates an end-to-end analytics workflow, from data inspection and cleaning to SQL analysis, dashboard development, and business interpretation.

### Project Details

| Item | Description |
|---|---|
| Project Name | Resume Screening & Recruitment Analytics |
| Project Type | Data Analytics and Business Intelligence |
| Domain | Recruitment Analytics |
| Dataset Size | Approximately 200,000 candidate records |
| Programming Language | Python |
| Data Analysis | Pandas and NumPy |
| Database | PostgreSQL |
| Query Language | SQL |
| Visualization Tool | Microsoft Power BI |
| Calculation Language | DAX |
| Project Status | In Progress — update when appropriate |

## 2. Business Problem

Organizations need to understand candidate profiles and review hiring outcomes to improve recruitment reporting and identify areas for further investigation.

Candidate records may include education, CGPA, experience, internships, projects, certifications, and skills scores. Analyzing these characteristics alongside recorded hiring outcomes can help stakeholders understand how outcomes vary across candidate groups.

Without organized analysis, it may be difficult to compare groups consistently, identify data-quality issues, or communicate results clearly.

This project addresses the problem by using Python, SQL, and Power BI to organize candidate data, calculate recruitment-related metrics, and present the findings through interactive visualizations.

**Business objective:** Provide a clear, data-driven overview of candidate characteristics and recorded hiring outcomes while recognizing the limitations of the available data.

## 3. Project Objectives

The main objectives are to:

1. Understand the structure and quality of the candidate dataset.
2. Clean and prepare data using Python and Pandas.
3. Perform exploratory data analysis to understand candidate characteristics.
4. Use SQL to analyze hiring outcomes across different candidate groups.
5. Develop KPIs and measures using DAX.
6. Build an interactive Power BI dashboard.
7. Identify meaningful patterns and communicate business insights.
8. Document the analytical process in a reproducible GitHub repository.
9. Demonstrate practical skills relevant to Data Analyst and Business Intelligence internships.

