## 11. Key Performance Indicators

The following DAX measures can be used in Power BI, assuming the data model contains a table named `Candidates` and the required columns.

### Total Candidates

```dax
Total Candidates =
COUNTROWS(Candidates)
```

### Selected Candidates

```dax
Selected Candidates =
CALCULATE(
    COUNTROWS(Candidates),
    Candidates[hired] = 1
)
```

### Not Selected Candidates

```dax
Not Selected Candidates =
CALCULATE(
    COUNTROWS(Candidates),
    Candidates[hired] = 0
)
```

### Selection Rate

```dax
Selection Rate =
DIVIDE(
    [Selected Candidates],
    [Total Candidates],
    0
)
```

Format this measure as a percentage.

### Average Experience

```dax
Average Experience =
AVERAGE(Candidates[experience_years])
```

### Average CGPA

```dax
Average CGPA =
AVERAGE(Candidates[cgpa])
```

### Average Skills Score

```dax
Average Skills Score =
AVERAGE(Candidates[skills_score])
```

### Average Projects

```dax
Average Projects =
AVERAGE(Candidates[projects])
```

### Average Internships

```dax
Average Internships =
AVERAGE(Candidates[internships])
```

The measures respond to relevant report filters. Validate them against equivalent Python or SQL calculations and consider how missing or invalid outcomes are handled.

